<article class="env-corollary" id="BE2649">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/BE2649">Corollary <span data-tag="BE2649">8.2.9.24</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a small category. Suppose that there exists a well-ordering $\leq $ on the collection of objects of $\calC $ satisfying the following condition: for every pair of objects $X,Y \in \calC $, we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Hom _{\calC }(X,Y) = \begin{cases} \emptyset &amp;  \text{ if } $X > Y$ \\ \{  \id _ X \}  &amp;  \text{ if } X = Y. \end{cases} \]
</div>
  <p> Let $\mathbf{A}$ be a model category. Then: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(i)$"><p>
A natural transformation $F \rightarrow G$ in $\Fun (\calC , \mathbf{A})$ is a (trivial) projective cofibration if and only if, for every object $C \in \calC $, the induced map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  F(C) \coprod _{ \varinjlim _{ D \rightarrow C, D \neq C} F(D) } \varinjlim _{ D \rightarrow C, D \neq C} G(D) \rightarrow G(C) \]
</div>
<p>
 is a (trivial) cofibration in $\mathbf{A}$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(ii)$"><p>
A natural transformation $F \rightarrow G$ in $\Fun (\calC ^{op}, \mathbf{A})$ is a (trivial) injective fibration if and only if, for every object $C \in \calC $, the induced map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  F(C) \rightarrow G(C) \times _{ \varprojlim _{D \rightarrow C, D \neq C} G(D) } \varprojlim _{D \rightarrow C, D \neq C} F(D)  \]
</div>
<p>
 is a (trivial) fibration in $\mathbf{A}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Example <a href="/tag/A16A1E" data-tag="A16A1E">8.2.9.22</a> with Proposition <a href="/tag/EDC2F7" data-tag="EDC2F7">8.2.9.19</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>